# Git commit messages

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

Format:

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <subject>
```

- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
- Subject: imperative mood, no trailing period, first line at most 72 characters
- One logical change per commit; do not mix feat and chore unless they are inseparable
- Do not skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless the user explicitly asks
- Pass the message with a HEREDOC, never `git commit -i`

Examples:

```
feat: add actix-web hello world HTTP server
chore: ignore build artifacts and editor files
ci: run fmt, clippy, tests, coverage, and audit
```
